# EverWeb Project Contract

- Treat `docs/architecture/EverWeb_Architecture_v2.2_Kimi_First.md` as the current canonical design.
- Before implementation, identify the relevant document section, architecture invariant (`INV-*`), implementation week, and Definition of Done.
- Inspect the current implementation and tests before editing. Do not rely on the design document alone when code already exists.
- Implement only the requested vertical slice. Do not add adjacent features, speculative abstractions, or unrelated cleanup.
- Do not invent values for fields marked `Unknown`, `None`, or `PendingTemplate`. Keep unresolved competition semantics isolated behind `CompetitionAdapter`.
- Prefer explicit domain types, receipts, and ports over untyped dictionaries or cross-layer shortcuts.
- Every production behavior change requires proportionate automated tests. A passing test does not excuse violating an architecture invariant.
- Do not weaken contracts, gates, security checks, or tests to make an implementation pass.
- If code, tests, and the canonical design disagree, stop and report the conflict instead of silently choosing one.
- Before completion, run the available targeted checks and report changed files, verification evidence, and unresolved specification gaps.
- Do not run `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks for that action in the current turn. Plan/todo deliver steps and "implementation complete" language alone are not permission.
